sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant MQ as RabbitMQ
    participant C as Consumer (Order or Inventory Service)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL (its schema)
    participant DLQ as Service DLQ (RabbitMQ)
    MQ->>C: deliver message (MessageId m)
    C-xPG: one transaction: business change + Inbox row m: write fails
    Note over C: not acknowledged, the consumer retries after 1 s
    alt the fault clears within the retry window
        C->>PG: retry succeeds: applied once
        C-->>MQ: ack
    else the fault outlasts 4 attempts (1 s, 2 s, 4 s apart)
        C-->>DLQ: nack without requeue: dead-lettered, x-death names the source queue
        Note over DLQ: only this service's DLQ, the main queue is empty, no loop
        DLQ->>MQ: after the fix, the dead letter is replayed unchanged
        MQ->>C: deliver m again
        C->>PG: applied once
    end
    Note over C,DLQ: malformed JSON or an empty MessageId is dead-lettered after one attempt
